            "/work/dusk": "amber",
            "/work/pearl": "Keep old practice rollback",
            "/work/example-note": "Keep this practice note.\n"
          },
          "stdout": "Practice changed\n",
          "stderr": "",
          "status": 0,
          "after": {
            "/work/plum": "violet\n",
            "/work/dusk": "violet\n",
            "/work/pearl": "amber",
            "/work/example-note": "Keep this practice note.\n"
          }
        }
      },
      "sources": [
        "https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/Command-Substitution.html",
        "https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/Bash-Builtins.html",
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-101-102-objectives/"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Only bounded valid UTF8/nonNUL flat virtual text files; no host execution, arbitrary binary cmp conformance, file metadata or modification counters. Same/different is exact text-byte equality, not Unicode normalization. No directories, links, tempfiles, rename, locking, traps, real clock, races or guaranteed Stop/resource rollback. Predictable preflight refusals preserve every file. Examples and drafts are isolated.",
      "retry_guidance": "Read the selected outcome and complete file differences. Check LF boundaries and error priority before changing publication logic; use a separate example to investigate."
